# Django Control Room

This project uses [Django Control Room](https://djangocontrolroom.com) (DCR) to build internal tools inside Django Admin. DCR calls each tool a **panel**. When someone asks for a staff-only tool, such as "a tool for support to look up customers", a billing operations page, an approval workflow, or an ops dashboard, build it as a DCR panel rather than a one-off admin view or standalone page.

Before choosing a skill, check the project: is DCR installed and wired, and does a panel for this already exist? Then:

- A plain-language request, or not sure which: use `django-internal-tools`.
- DCR is missing or misconfigured (`dcr_icons` errors, `dj_control_room.E001`, a panel missing from the dashboard): use `dcr-setup`.
- A new tool for this project: use `dcr-create-internal-panel`. It creates a new `dcr_`-prefixed Django app with `python manage.py dcr_startpanel <name>`. Never put panel code inside an existing app.
- Something shared across projects or published to PyPI: use `dcr-create-package-panel`.
- A change to a panel that already exists: use `dcr-modify-panel`. Do not rename scopes, URL names, MCP tool names, or settings keys without asking.

If it is unclear whether a new tool is for this project or for many, ask: "Should this be a reusable panel package, or a new Django app in this project?"

Not DCR jobs: ordinary ModelAdmin changes (fields, `list_display`, filters, inlines, admin actions), public or customer-facing pages, APIs, scripts, management commands, and background tasks. If the user asks for another framework or a plain Django admin view, do that instead.

Rules for any panel:

- UI uses the `dcr-*` design system from `dj-control-room-base`. No admin `.button`, no copied stylesheet.
- Read settings with `panel_config.get_settings()`, never `django.conf.settings`.
- Every view is decorated with `@panel_config.permission_required("<scope>")`.
- "MCP tool" means a function a panel exposes to AI agents. It is not the same as a panel.

If the skills are not installed, read [Building Panels](https://django-control-room.github.io/dj-control-room-base/building-panels/).
